%C - 9P2000.L filesystem client for QEMU virtio-9p shares (version @PROJECT_VERSION@)

%C [-o option[,option...]] mount_tag mount_point

Mounts the host directory that QEMU exports with mount_tag
(-device virtio-9p-device,...,mount_tag=TAG on the aarch64 virt machine)
at mount_point, then runs in the background.

Options:
 ro           Mount read-only
 rw           Mount read-write (the default)
 cache=MS     Keep file attributes and failed lookups for MS milliseconds
              (default 0: always ask the host). Changes made on the host
              may show up to MS late; file contents are never cached.
 msize=N      Largest 9P message to ask for, in bytes (default 524288)
 requests=N   9P requests in flight at once, 1-8 (default 4); each one
              takes 2 x msize of memory
 timeout=MS   Give up on a request after MS milliseconds, 0 = never
              (default 30000)
 debug        Stay in the foreground; log setup and every 9P message
 poll         Poll for completions instead of using the interrupt (debug)
 irq=N        Use interrupt N instead of the one the device slot implies

Unmount with 'slay fs-9p'. Without root, fs-9p needs the abilities
mem_phys, interrupt and pathspace. Full documentation:
share/doc/fs-9p/html/index.html under the installation prefix.

Examples:
 fs-9p hostshare /mnt/host
 fs-9p -o ro,cache=2000 tools /opt/tools
 on -u user -A nonroot,allow,mem_phys -A nonroot,allow,interrupt \
    -A nonroot,allow,pathspace fs-9p hostshare /mnt/host
